      "The 39% figure rests on 48 modelled voices (about two per group), so it shows direction more than a forecast; real attrition could fall noticeably less, and differences between groups (e.g. women -40% vs men -38%) are too small to act on.",
      "The positive reaction depends on employees believing the voices' claim that home days 'don't cost me anything at work'; if managers informally favour in-office faces in reviews or promotions, the goodwill and the retention gain could reverse.",
